From f06ec6b934526e0afe26263411276d3205d3cdbe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anselm Busse <anselm.busse@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 00:00:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 30/49] x86_64/k1om: keep the libpthread symbol versions
 dropped upstream

Upstream removed libpthread symbols such as nanosleep@GLIBC_2.2.5 or
open@GLIBC_2.2.5 once libc exported the same name@version, which holds
on x86_64 but not on K1OM, whose libc starts at GLIBC_2.14: binaries
built against MPSS 3.8.6 stop resolving them.  Keep them in libpthread
as tail-call stubs to the libc functions.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Anselm Busse <anselm.busse@outlook.com>
